#: ../../../accordions.md:3
msgid "Accordions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:5
msgid ""
"An `accordion` groups a set of [dropdowns](sd-dropdowns) so that they behave "
"as one *exclusive* set: opening one item automatically closes the others. "
"This is useful for FAQ-style content, where only one answer should be "
"visible at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:9
msgid ""
"The behaviour is native to HTML and requires **no JavaScript**: the "
"directive simply gives every item a shared `name`, and the browser does the "
"rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:0
msgid "What is an accordion?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:15
msgid "A container of dropdowns where opening one collapses the others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:0
msgid "How do I add one?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:19
msgid ""
"Nest `dropdown` directives inside an `accordion` directive (see the syntax "
"below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:0
msgid "Does it need JavaScript?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:24
msgid ""
"No. It uses the native `name` attribute shared across `<details>` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:0
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr "語法"

#: ../../../accordions.md:31
msgid ""
"::::{accordion}\n"
"\n"
":::{dropdown} First item\n"
"Opening another item closes this one.\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{dropdown} Second item\n"
":open:\n"
"\n"
"Content of the second item.\n"
":::\n"
"\n"
":::{dropdown} Third item\n"
"Content of the third item.\n"
":::\n"
"::::\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:34
msgid ""
".. accordion::\n"
"\n"
"    .. dropdown:: First item\n"
"\n"
"        Opening another item closes this one.\n"
"\n"
"    .. dropdown:: Second item\n"
"        :open:\n"
"\n"
"        Content of the second item.\n"
"\n"
"    .. dropdown:: Third item\n"
"\n"
"        Content of the third item.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:40
msgid "The `:open:` interaction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:42
msgid ""
"Because only one item in an exclusive group can be open at a time, you may "
"mark **at most one** child dropdown with the [`:open:`](sd-dropdowns) "
"option, to have the accordion start with that item expanded. If several "
"items are marked `:open:`, only the first is kept open (the rest are "
"collapsed and a `design.accordion` warning is emitted)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:48
msgid "Flush variant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../accordions.md:50
msgid ""
"Add the `:flush:` flag for an edge-to-edge look (like Bootstrap's *accordion-"
"flush*): the outer side borders and corner rounding are removed, so the "
"accordion blends into its parent container."
msgstr ""

